issue(id="0016" status="review")
  title Canonicalize inline attributes to space-separated form
  user-story
    as-a maintainer of puggers
    i-want inline attributes to format in a more idiomatic Pug style
    so-that canonical output matches common Pug conventions without unnecessary punctuation
  premise.
    The formatter previously canonicalized inline attribute separators to commas,
    even though Pug treats commas as optional and common examples use simple
    space-separated attributes. That comma style predated the whitespace tasks,
    but it proved less desirable as the default canonical output. The formatter
    now prefers single-space separators between inline attributes while still
    accepting commas, spaces, tabs, and newlines in the input.
  acceptance-criteria
    criterion Format inline attribute lists with single spaces between attributes in canonical output.
    criterion Continue to accept comma-, space-, tab-, and newline-separated attribute input without parse regressions.
    criterion Keep wrapped multiline attribute layout behavior unchanged.
    criterion Rebaseline checked-in docs and tests so canonical fixtures match the new attribute style.
  review-items
    item(status="covered") Inline attribute formatting now emits space-separated canonical output instead of commas.
    item(status="covered") Attribute, whitespace-normalization, line-width, and docs-idempotence coverage all pass with the new style.
    item(status="covered") The checked-in Pug docs under `docs/pug/2026-05-31` have been reformatted to the new canonical attribute style.
